			<div class="content" id="post-content-1991458">
									

<p>This is one of the hardest upvotes I've ever settled upon, so I'll go through my thought processes.</p>
<p>The first, of course was, &quot;Oh, great, everyone's doing Thaumiel now&quot; but it's just Roget, so <em>I guess that's okay I guess</em>. (Why do we even keep records on Thaumiel objects, though? If they're intrinsic to Foundation secrets, shouldn't they all have huge ACCESS DENIED warning signs on them?)</p>
<p>Second was some appreciation for the image, the theme, and &quot;Foundation Thaumaturgists&quot;, because seriously, wtf.</p>
<p>Third was a certain disdain for the Foundation creating a skip that finds other skips. This was mitigated entirely by the project being retired. (And I do like the old containment procedures.)</p>
<p>I was a little iffy on the interview, because it starts off like &quot;standard crazy people talk&quot;, but there does seem to be something going on and it gets pretty niftily creepy by the end. Having internal logic is key to making crazy people talk work.</p>
<p>What's most conflicting, though, is the final part. I mean, having this be the thing that predicts/causes Dr. Bright's bonding with 963 is extremely cheesy, not to mention one of those &quot;Do we even <em>do</em> this anymore?&quot; moments. The only way I can think to put it is it feels Series I, and not in a good way. (Also wow, I hadn't upvoted 963, wtf.) Plus, I think this could straight-up exist without that part and be just fine.</p>
<p>So I'm actually not sure why I upvoted now, but I'll leave it to avoid seeming contrarian.</p>

